  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Knowledge &amp; Education Evidence Products (KEEP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This programme will secure UK leadership to produce global goods in education, catalyse mulitlateral, bilateral and philanthropic spend to address learning poverty,  and convene global and national policy reform events across 27 DFID countries. Funding will support research projects which respond to the urgent need to understand how to bring girls back into the classroom following Covid-19 school closures, and informs systems change to ensure all children can learn once they return to school. This programme directly responds to the manifesto commitment on girls&apos; education.</narrative>
  </description>
